DONE

  - Repository, README, ROADMAP.md, and the ideas, arch, plans and bugs
    folders with their README files; MangoWM and Hyprland evaluations.
  - Fresh code, not a fork. Taken, rewritten and listed in UPSTREAM.md:
    MangoWM's dwindle tree and tag view model, Hyprland's dwindle split
    rules, and the layer-shell protocol file.
  - No globals: one tp_server is passed everywhere. Each module owns and
    removes its own listeners, so teardown never trips wlroots' destroy
    assertions.
  - The dwindle tree is pure: opaque items, settings kept in the tree,
    windows placed through a callback. It is unit-testable, and Lua
    layouts can reuse it.
  - Bindings match the unshifted key symbol, so "Meta+Shift+1" is written
    with "1" on any layout.
  - Windows are configured only on a real size change, saving redraws.
  - The event loop never blocks: tp_spawn double-forks.
  - Dropped: scenefx, pango, cairo, cJSON, pcre2, xcb, meson and ninja.
    Direct dependencies: wlroots 0.20, wayland-server, xkbcommon, libtam
    (static), libc and libm.
  - tools/pull-references keeps the MangoWM and Hyprland clones current,
    from the list in ideas/sources.
  - Checked: make clean && make has no warnings with -Wall -Wextra
    -Wpedantic. make test passes: test_tags (28 checks), test_dwindle (52
    checks), and the headless smoke test (starts, opens its socket, maps
    two foot windows, survives one closing, exits 0 on SIGTERM).
    readelf -d lists only libwlroots-0.20, libwayland-server,
    libxkbcommon, libm and libc.


